<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;"><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Dear {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
&nbsp;</span></span></span><br />
<span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">On behalf of Qantas, I apologise for the disruption caused as a result of an engineering issue on QF2 from Singapore to Sydney on 3 Sept 22.<br />
<br />
As you may be aware, there was an issue with one of the emergency slides on the upper deck of the aircraft which prevented us from using the full Business cabin for safety reasons. Our engineers attempted to fix the issue to allow all passengers to travel as planned however unfortunately, they weren’t able to do so.<br />
<br />
The safety of our passengers and crew is always Qantas' top priority, however, we appreciate the disappointment and frustration this caused being unable to travel in our Business class cabin.<br />
<br />
As you were unable to travel as planned, you are entitled to a partial refund of your fare. &nbsp;We will be shortly processing your refund to your travel agent.<br />
<br />
In addition, as an apology, we would like to offer you XXXXXXX. &nbsp;Please provide your bank details for us to process this for you.<br />
<br />
Additionally, if you incurred any other travel expenses as a result of this disruption that you would like to claim, simply respond to this email with copies of the receipts and we will consider them.<br />
<br />
Once again, we do apologise for the inconvenience caused and thank you for your ongoing support.</span></span></span></body>
